Skill	craft:github
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; cat $D/take-in.md; ls $D/scripts
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; cat $D/tracker.md | head -80; echo ----; bash $D/scripts/take-in-check.sh 91; echo "exit=$?"
Bash	gh issue view 91 --json title,body,assignees
text	**#91 README: the install command says npm instal**  The README tells the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so the command fails. The work is done when the README says `npm install shop`.  I have not taken the issue yet. The take-in check found an existing branch for it:  ``` #91: branch fix/91-typo, 0 commits ahead of main, last commit 2026-11-03T00:00:00Z ```  Nobody is assigned to #91. The branch `fix/91-typo` exists, but it has no commits past `main`. GitHub does not record who owns a branch.  **Whose branch is `fix/91-typo`?** If it is someone else's, I will stop here. If it is yours, I will next ask whether the work runs somewhere else or continues here.
